## Spec-Driven Development

This project uses **{{ 'Spec-Kit' if sdd_framework == 'spec-kit' else 'OpenSpec' }}** for non-trivial features. For tasks that touch >3
files, change a schema, or rebuild a pipeline, **start from a spec, not a chat**.
The full workflow lives in `docs/how-to/spec-driven-development.md`.

{% if sdd_framework == 'spec-kit' -%}
- Spec artefacts live under `.specify/specs/<feature>/`.
- Precedence on conflict: **Constitution > spec.md > plan.md > tasks.md > code**.
- Tasks marked `[P]` may run in parallel.
{%- else -%}
- Active changes live under `openspec/changes/<change>/`; archived specs under `openspec/specs/`.
- `openspec/AGENTS.md` is the project-wide constitution — read before `/opsx:propose`.
- Delta markers (`ADDED`/`MODIFIED`/`REMOVED`) make the contract change explicit.
{%- endif %}
