## Codex CLI specifics
{%- if codex_provider == 'subscription' %}

- **Auth:** run `codex login` once (ChatGPT account).
{%- else %}

- **Auth:** export `OPENAI_API_KEY=<litellm-token>` and
  `OPENAI_BASE_URL={{ litellm_base_url }}` in your shell — never commit either.
  Default model: `gpt-5.5` (pinned in `.codex/config.toml`).
{%- endif %}

- Codex reads `AGENTS.md` natively. Config lives in `.codex/config.toml`:
  `model = "gpt-5.5"`, `sandbox_mode = "workspace-write"`,
  `approval_policy = "on-request"`, `model_reasoning_effort = "medium"`,
  `default_permissions = ":workspace"`. For CI use flags on `codex exec`,
  not config overrides.
- **Subagents** (`.codex/agents/*.toml`, referenced in `config.toml`):
  `researcher` (recon), `reviewer` (independent diff review), `security-auditor`.
  Parity with Claude Code / OpenCode. Subagents cannot spawn subagents.
- **Memory:** `features.memories = true` (Chronicle) is the private tier —
  Codex manages it natively. Team memory is `guidelines/*.md` + this file.
  Use `/capture` to promote a private learning into team memory.
- **Verify-on-Stop:** a `Stop` hook (`.codex/hooks/verify-on-stop.sh`) reminds
  about `just qa` when a session ends with uncommitted diff. Set
  `CODEX_VERIFY_HARD_BLOCK=1` for a hard gate before the turn can end.
- **Context:** `/statusline` and `/status` are built-in. Install
  [`ccusage`](https://ccusage.com/guide/codex/) (`npm i -g ccusage`) for token/cost
  tracking. `/compact` around ~70 % context usage; `/clear` on topic switch.
{%- if include_context7 %}
- **Context7** is enabled (opt-in): `[mcp_servers.context7]` in `.codex/config.toml`
  fetches current library docs. Requires Node on PATH; queries leave the sandbox.
{%- else %}
- **Optional MCP:** Context7 is commented out — re-enable via `include_context7`
  if you want current library docs in-context. Avoid filesystem / git / github
  MCPs — `gh` and shell are 4–32× cheaper per task.
{%- endif %}
- **Permissions:** Codex uses the `:workspace` sandbox profile. Maschinelles
  Bash-Deny ist nicht aktiviert (Codex' execpolicy deny-Syntax ist noch nicht
  TOML-stabil); die Verbote aus `shared_deny_bash` gelten verbal via this file,
  und pre-commit (`gitleaks`, `detect-private-key`) ist die harte Backstop-Ebene.
{%- endif %}
