## Aider specifics
{%- if aider_provider == 'litellm' %}

- **Auth (LiteLLM):**
  - `.aider.conf.yml` already pins `openai-api-base: {{ litellm_base_url }}` —
    do not edit per-machine.
  - In your shell (never committed): `export OPENAI_API_KEY=$LITELLM_TOKEN`.
  - Default model: `{{ aider_model }}`.
{%- else %}

- **Auth (Ollama):** none — the local daemon at `{{ ollama_base_url }}` is keyless.
  Pre-pull the model: `ollama pull {{ aider_model | replace('ollama/', '') }}`.
  Default model: `{{ aider_model }}`.
{%- endif %}

- Run with `aider` — `AGENTS.md` and `guidelines/*.md` are loaded automatically (`read:` in `.aider.conf.yml`).
- `auto-commits` is disabled: stage and commit yourself after reviewing each diff.
- **Memory:** `read:` in `.aider.conf.yml` loads `AGENTS.md` + `guidelines/*.md` as
  static project memory (team tier). Aider has no native dynamic memory; use
  `/capture` to promote a learning into `guidelines/*.md`.
- **No native permission system.** Unlike Claude Code (`.claude/settings.json`)
  and OpenCode (`opencode.json`), Aider has no built-in bash-deny or file-deny
  enforcement. The guardrails in this file plus `pre-commit` (`gitleaks`,
  `detect-private-key`) are the only safety net — review every diff manually
  before staging.
- **Context7** is not available for Aider (no MCP support).
{%- endif %}
