## OpenCode specifics

- **Backend:** Ollama daemon at `{{ ollama_base_url }}` — the daemon is the proxy for
  *both* local and `:cloud`-tagged models.
{%- if tier == 'local' %}
- **Tier:** local. No auth, no API keys — this project's air-gapped option.
  Pre-pull the workhorse + small_model:
  - `ollama pull qwen3-coder:30b` *(MoE 30B-A3B, q4_K_M, ~19 GB; on 48 GB unified memory consider `qwen3-coder:30b-a3b-q8_0` ~32 GB for less quant loss)*
  - `ollama pull qwen3:4b`
{%- elif tier == 'cloud' %}
- **Tier:** cloud. Run `ollama signin` once; the daemon forwards `:cloud` models
  to Ollama Cloud transparently. Default large = `glm-5.2:cloud`, small_model =
  `gpt-oss:20b-cloud`.
{%- else %}
- **Tier:** hybrid. Cloud frontier model as the large default
  (`glm-5.2:cloud`), local Qwen3 4B as `small_model` for utility tasks
  (title gen, compaction). Setup: `ollama signin` for cloud auth + `ollama
  pull qwen3:4b` for the local utility.
{%- endif %}
- Switch model in-session with `/model <name>` — the `models:` block in
  `opencode.json` lists the available choices. `provider.ollama.small_model`
  drives title generation / summarisation / sub-tools — keep it cheap.
- Two primary modes: `plan` (architect, read-only) and `build` (coder). Switch with `Tab`.
- Read-only subagents live in `.opencode/agents/` — `@reviewer` (independent diff
  review), `@researcher` (recon, context-isolated), `@security-auditor`. Address
  them with `@<name>` in chat or let `build` auto-delegate via the `task` tool.
  Offload verbose recon/tests to them to keep the main context clean.
- **Memory:** OpenCode has no native dynamic memory. The `instructions` array in
  `opencode.json` loads `AGENTS.md` + `guidelines/*.md` as static project memory
  (team tier). Use `/capture` to promote a learning into `guidelines/*.md`.
{%- if include_opencode_learning_inbox %}
  When `include_opencode_learning_inbox` is on, the Learning-Inbox adds a
  project-local private tier: `.opencode/LEARNINGS.md` (canonical, in context
  via `instructions:`) + `.opencode/LEARNINGS.inbox.md` (staging, not in
  context). A SessionEnd plugin (`capture-learnings.ts`) auto-extracts
  proposals via `small_model`; `/capture review` promotes manually. Disable
  via `OPENCODE_LEARNINGS_MIN_BYTES=0`. See
  `docs/explanation/learning-loop.md`.
{%- endif %}
- `permission` block in `opencode.json` uses granular object syntax: denies
  destructive bash patterns (`rm -rf`, `sudo`, `curl|bash`), denies writes to
  guardrail files (`shared_deny_write`), denies reads of secrets (`.env`,
  `*.pem`), and asks before `git push` / hard-reset / rebase. `doom_loop` is
  set to `ask`. That file is the SPOT for runtime tool glue; consult it, don't
  restate it here.
{%- if include_context7 %}
- **Context7** is enabled (opt-in): `mcp.context7` in `opencode.json` fetches
  current library docs. External service (`mcp.context7.com`) — queries leave
  the sandbox.
{%- endif %}
- **Verify-on-stop plugin** (`.opencode/plugins/verify-on-stop.ts`) reminds about
  `just qa` when a session ends with uncommitted diff. Hard-block opt-in via
  `OPENCODE_VERIFY_HARD_BLOCK=1`. Plugin API is experimental — may change.
- **Token/cost tracking:** opencode logs per-session usage; for an out-of-process
  dashboard use [`opencode-quota`](https://github.com/slkiser/opencode-quota) or
  [`tokscale`](https://github.com/junhoyeo/tokscale) — both avoid context-window
  pollution. `/compact` around ~70 % usage; `/clear` on topic switch.
{%- endif %}
